---
description: Project rules for Triage Console v2
alwaysApply: true
---

# Source of truth
- PLAN.md is the spec. Read the sections named in the task before coding.
- If the task conflicts with PLAN.md or is ambiguous, stop and ask. Do not guess silently.
- You are acting as a senior product designer and a Palo Alto Networks TAC engineer with 15 years in network security. Domain details (PAN-OS CLI output, log fields, IKE/IPsec behaviour, policy evaluation order) must be technically correct.

# Never ship broken flows
- Client-only Vite SPA. No server rendering.
- Every route must render real seeded data. Empty with seeded data = bug.
- Guard every lookup: if an id is not found, render a designed not-found state with a way back. Never throw.
- Every route has an error boundary with a designed fallback and a "Back to Tickets" action.
- localStorage and sessionStorage access always in try/catch.
- Every button does something real or is visibly disabled with a reason. No dead buttons.

# Scope
- Build only what the current phase asks. No extra features or abstractions.
- No backend, no real auth. Demo login is client-side only.
- Never read the real clock for data. Use src/lib/time.ts (Tue 6 Oct 2026, 12:05 IST).
- Case state lives only in src/lib/case-engine.ts. Console, tools, logs, network status, and thread read from it.

# Code
- TypeScript strict, no `any`. Shared types in src/types.ts.
- Small components with one job. Copy lives in src/content.
- Every changed line traces to the task. Do not refactor or reformat unrelated code. Mention dead code, do not delete it.

# Design
- Only tokens from PLAN.md section 7. No raw hex in components.
- Geist Sans for UI, Geist Mono for technical values only.
- Sentence case. No all-caps labels. No em dashes or en dashes in any copy or docs.
- Priority and status never by color alone.
- Motion only on user action, except the splash. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Keyboard reachable, visible focus, aria labels on icon buttons.
- Loading, empty, and error states on every data view.
- No Palo Alto Networks logos or trademarks in UI chrome.

# Verification (required before saying done)
1. `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm test` pass.
2. `npm run build` then `npm run e2e` (Playwright against `vite preview`) pass.
3. Playwright saves screenshots at 1440x900 of every screen touched to tests/e2e/screens/. Open and review them. List anything that looks unpolished and fix it.
4. Report: what changed, which tests prove it, screenshots reviewed, anything still open.
